#### Di-electron decays of vector mesons

In this section, we will discuss the di-electron decays of vector mesons and mainly consider \(\omega\) and \(\phi\) contribution. The same method as di-electron cocktail studying [107] was used. The algorithm is at the below:

* Get \(M_{e^{+}e^{-}}\) spectra and invariant yields of \(\omega\to e^{+}e^{-}/\pi^{0}e^{+}e^{-}\) and \(\phi\to e^{+}e^{-}/\eta e^{+}e^{-}\) from simulation:
* Use the Tsallis function fittings from measured invariant yields of \(\omega\) and \(\phi\) as input to a detector simulation.
* The particles are decayed into di-electrons with the appropriate branch ratio by using the formula: \[\frac{dN}{dM_{e^{+}e^{-}}}\propto\sqrt{1-\frac{4m_{e}{}^{2}}{M_{e^{+}e^{-}} }}(1+\frac{2m_{e}{}^{2}}{M_{e^{+}e^{-}}})\frac{1}{M_{e^{+}e^{-}}}(1-\frac{M_{ e^{+}e^{-}}}{M_{h}{}^{2}})^{3}|F(M_{e^{+}e^{-}})|^{2}.\] (3.12)
* Get \(M_{e^{+}e^{-}}\) spectrum and invariant yield of \(c\overline{c}\) (charm and anti-charm quark) \(\to e^{+}e^{-}\) using PYTHIA6.416.
* Require \(|y_{e^{+}e^{-}}|<1\), \(|\eta_{e}|<0.7\), \(p_{T}(e)>0.2\) GeV/\(c\) and \(M_{e^{+}e^{-}}>0.15\) GeV/\(c\).
* Normalize \(M_{e^{+}e^{-}}\) spectra (only checked our result with the published one [107]) and invariant yields using the \(dN/dy\) and branch ratio of \(\omega,\phi\) and \(c\).

The invariant yields of \(\omega\to e\), \(\phi\to e\) and \(c\to e\) from simulation are shown in the left panel of Fig. 3.23. According to the invariant yields, the ratios of electrons from \(\omega\) and \(\phi\) decays than charm quark hadrons decay to electrons were obtained, which are shown in the right panel of Fig. 3.23.

