#### Trigger/Vertex bias correction

In our analysis, the event selections required a VPD coincidence and a valid primary vertex finding. So the measured NPE cross-section should be calculated as:

\[E\frac{d^{3}\sigma}{d^{3}p} =\frac{1}{L}\frac{1}{2\pi\text{p}_{T}dp_{T}dy}\frac{N^{raw}_{NPE }}{\epsilon^{track\_level}_{NPE}\epsilon^{VPD\_coincidence}_{NPE}}\epsilon^{ GoodVeteX}_{NPE} \tag{3.13}\] \[=\frac{\sigma_{SND}}{\frac{N^{VPD\_coincidence\&\&GoodVetex}_{NPE }}{\frac{N^{VPD\_coincidence\&\GoodVetex}_{NPE}}{\epsilon^{track\_level}_{NPE }}\epsilon^{VPD\_coincidence\&\GoodVetex}_{NPE}}}\] \[=\frac{\sigma_{SND}}{N^{VPD\_coincidence\&\&GoodVetex}_{NPE}} \frac{1}{2\pi\text{p}_{T}dp_{T}dy}\frac{N^{raw}_{NPE}}{\epsilon^{track\_level}_{ NPE}}\epsilon^{VPD\_coincidence\&\GoodVetex}_{NPE}\] \[=\frac{\sigma_{SND}}{N^{VPD\_coincidence\&\&\GoodVetex}_{NPE}} \frac{1}{2\pi\text{p}_{T}dp_{T}dy}\frac{N^{raw}_{NPE}}{\epsilon^{track\_level}_{ NPE}}f_{trigger/vertex\_bias},\]

where \(L\) is the luminosity and \(\sigma_{NSD}\) is the non-singly diffractive (NSD) cross section, which is obtained by \(\sigma^{pp}_{inel}/R_{\sigma}\). The pp inelastic cross section \(\sigma^{pp}_{inel}=42\,mb\)[110] and the factor \(R_{\sigma}=1.4\). Due to the VPD coincidence and valid primary vertex finding are both different between NPE event and MB event. This causes the trigger/vertex bias (last fraction of the above formula) of NPE event because we used MB data to study NPE cross-section. Because of the VPD limited acceptance, NPE event has more tracks at the mid-rapidity than MB event. Thus the VPD coincidence efficiency of NPE event

